id: earthquake-weather
name: Earthquake Weather
kind: battlefield
weather: true
profile: elemental-earth
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The ground itself. Might 1(WT) lower, Defense Value halved past Natural, and knocked
  Prone every Combat Round at Cataclysmic - and none of it touches you off the ground.
text: >
  Earthquake Weather: The ground beneath your feet rumbles, shakes, and splits open,
  endangering everyone for miles around.

  Connected Profile: Elemental (Earth)

  Natural Weather (Tier 1) Effect(s):
  * While you are not in a High Environment, reduce your Might by 1(WT).

  Unnatural Weather (Tier 2) Effect(s):
  * While you are not in a High Environment, halve your Defense Value.

  Cataclysmic Weather (Tier 3) Effect(s):
  * At the start of each Combat Round, if you are not in a High Environment, you are
  knocked Prone.

---

# The one Weather that had to wait for the High Environments, and the reason it waited is
# written into all three of its effects: "while you are not in a High Environment". An
# earthquake is the ground shaking, and the ground cannot reach somebody who is not on it.
#
# --- Why this needs asking at all ------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Three of the four High Environments forbid Battle Weather outright, and a Weather that is
# forbidden is not gathered - so in the High Sky and above, these effects would never run
# whether they asked or not.
#
# The Low Sky is the exception and is the whole of why the question exists: it forbids no
# Weather, so an earthquake is still in play while a character hovers over it, and it is
# the test below that stops the ground shaking somebody standing in the air.
#
# `battlefield.highEnvironment == 0` is the test, and Rank 0 is the ground by the rules'
# own definition: "the typical Battle Environment that is not a High Environment is
# considered Rank 0."
#
# --- Natural (1) and Unnatural (2) --------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Might and the Defense Value, both while on the ground. Nested rather than written twice:
# the Tier test is inside the height test, because being off the ground turns the whole
# Weather off and there is no Tier at which it reaches you up there.
#
# The Might is 1(WT), so it is also what a Knockback throws with and how far - which is a
# quiet second effect the entry does not mention and follows from Might being one number.
#
# --- Cataclysmic (3) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "At the start of each Combat Round, if you are not in a High Environment, you are knocked
# Prone."
#
# The Round rather than the turn, so it lands once on everybody standing in it. No clock:
# the entry gives none, so Prone comes off the way Prone always comes off - by getting up,
# which is a thing you then have to do every Round.
#
# --- What is not built ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Connected Profile: Elemental (Earth)." The Elemental Profiles are the Magic Profiles,
# and there are none in this system yet. Carried in the header and read by nobody.

[passive]
if (battlefield.highEnvironment == 0) {
  might -= 1(WT);

  if (battlefield.weather.tier >= 2) {
    defenseValue *= 0.5;
  }
}

[automatic/start-of-round]
if (battlefield.highEnvironment == 0) {
  if (battlefield.weather.tier >= 3) {
    gain(prone);
  }
}
